=begin

Attempts to cast non-attack spells from your collection of scrolls,
vellums, parchments, etc. Utilizes separate containers to manage vibrant scrolls.
Checks your reserve slots first (invoked directly, no need to hold them), then
will rummage in your scrollsack for matching spell numbers, upon finding a vibrant
scroll it will place that scroll in your vibrantscrollsack unless usage of vibrant
scrolls is toggled on.

Invoke/casts normal scrolls.
Incants spells absorbed from vibrant scrolls.

Originally based on the work by Sulien on scrollbuff.lic, this script has been
almost entirely re-written to allow:
Invoking from either hand,
Support for vibrant ink scrolls,
Support for reserved scrolls,
Support for self-cast utility spells,
Configurable durations for stackable or refreshable spells

    author: Nihiladrem (todd.estabrooks@gmail.com)
      game: gs
      tags: invoke, scroll, scrolls, hunting
      version: 0.1.14

    CHANGELOG:
    0.1.14 - 0.1.13's reserve check re-tested every reserve item against every spell
             number, even ones already matched to a different spell -- spammy with a
             couple of reserve items and a long spell list (e.g. one item matched to
             spell 211, then re-tried and failing against every other spell requested
             after it). A reserve item's spell doesn't change during a run, so matches
             are now cached and reused instead of re-tested.
    0.1.13 - Added support for scrolls sitting in reserve slots (see ;reserve list) --
             these are invoked directly by id and never need to be picked up or put
             away. findscroll now checks reserve before rummaging any container, and
             returns [scrolltype, scrollid] (plus an already-completed invoke result
             for reserve hits, so castscroll doesn't invoke it twice) instead of
             leaving the caller to guess scrollid from checkright/checkleft -- which
             also fixes findscroll silently returning nil when vibrant use was toggled
             on and the very first rummage already found a normal (non-vibrant) scroll.
             The "That spell is not on the ..." retry in castscroll now also figures
             out which hand (if any) actually holds the failed scroll instead of
             assuming it's always in the right hand.
    0.1.12 - The 0.1.9 "no progress" cap check read timeleft right after casting, before
             the duration feed had caught up, so it mistook a normal update lag for
             hitting the real cap: it broke out of the incant loop early, then the outer
             loop re-invoked from the now-empty vibrant scroll ("That spell is not on
             the ..."), which put it in the wrong sack (always scrollsack, regardless of
             where it came from) and could try to put it away a second time at the end.
             The cap check now waits up to 3 seconds for the duration to update, the
             retry puts the scroll back in the sack matching its scrolltype, and the
             final put-away is skipped if the scroll isn't actually in a hand anymore.
    0.1.11 - Renamed the scrollbag/vibrantscrollbag vars to scrollsack/vibrantscrollsack
             to match the container vars used by fizzfuse.lic. Still set with
             ;vars set scrollsack=... and ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=...
    0.1.10 - Fixed the help/settings display always showing "Use vibrant Scrolls: No"
             regardless of the actual toggle: it compared scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle
             to "Yes", but the setting is stored as "True"/"False" everywhere else in
             the script.
    0.1.9 - Fixed infinite incant loop introduced in 0.1.8: the stacking loop compared
            timeleft > target_duration, but a spell can never exceed its own server-
            enforced cap, so once it reached max it looped forever (seen with 905
            stuck at its 4h10m cap). Comparisons now use >=, and as a second safety
            net the loop also stops if an incant doesn't actually add duration, in
            case the real server cap differs from the spell's declared max.
    0.1.8 - Vibrant ink scrolls grant temporary knowledge of the spell instead of
            consuming a scroll per cast, so stackable spells cast from a vibrant
            scroll now stack up to the spell's real maximum duration instead of
            stopping at stackto_duration. Refreshable and one-shot spells are
            unaffected since recasting them doesn't add duration.
    0.1.7 - Stopped findscroll from mutating SpellNumsNeeded with .shift, which removed
            the wrong spell (whatever was first in the list) whenever any scroll was
            missing, mislabeling successfully-cast spells as skipped. Final summary now
            separately lists spells cast, spells whose scroll wasn't found, and spells
            that weren't needed.
    0.1.6 - Fixed active-spell detection to use Spell.active/active? (like ewaggle.lic)
            instead of the raw spell.active attribute, and to compare each spell's
            remaining duration against the correct threshold for its type
            (stackable/refreshable/one-shot) instead of always using stackto.
    0.1.5 - Fixed an issue with scrolls being stored incorrectly in vibrantscrollsack
    0.1.4 - Fixed a bug with vibrant scroll casting
    0.1.3 - Changed logic to allow all non-attack spells.
    0.1.2 - Changed vars to scrollbag to avoid confusion, clarified help messaging.
    0.1.1 - Scrollbuff2 rework by Nihiladrem
    0.0.1 - Initial version by Sulien
    
=end

debug = false
## spell_num (string) => reserve item id, once a reserve scroll's fixed spell
## has been confirmed by invoking it. Reset each run since $ vars persist for
## the life of the Lich process. Global (not local) so findscroll, a top-level
## def, can see it without threading it through every call.
$scrollbuff3_reserve_matches = {}

def echofmt(*lines)
    maxlen = lines.map(&:length).max + 1
    echo "=" * maxlen
    lines.each do |line|
        echo line + (" " * (maxlen - line.length))
    end
    echo "=" * maxlen
end

##Check for empty hand
unless (checkright.nil?) ||  (checkleft.nil?)
    echofmt "Empty a hand and try again"
    exit
end

##Check for scrollsack
scrollsackVar = Vars["scrollsack"]
unless scrollsackVar
    echofmt "Please set your scroll container with a",
            "command like:",
            "    ;vars set scrollsack=silver backpack",
            "",
            "Use only a noun and optionally a single adjective.",
            "",
            "This will only work with containers you are",
            "wearing or holding."
    
    exit
end
scrollsack = GameObj[scrollsackVar]
unless scrollsack
    echofmt "Couldn't find your scrollsack \"#{scrollsackVar}\"",
            "Fetch that and try again, would ya?"
    
    exit
end
##Check for vibrantscrollsack
vibrantscrollsackVar = Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]
unless vibrantscrollsackVar
    echofmt "Please set your vibrant scroll container with a",
            "command like:",
            "    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=white satchel",
            "",
            "Use only a noun and optionally a single adjective.",
            "",
            "This will only work with containers you are",
            "wearing or holding.",
			"",
			"Your vibrantscrollsack needs to be a different",
			"than your scrollsack."
    exit
end

##Get duration settings
stackto_duration = CharSettings["scrollbuff-stackto"]
if debug == true; echo "Stack duration: #{stackto_duration}";end
if !(CharSettings["scrollbuff-stackto"].to_i > 0)
	if debug == true; echo "Warning! No stackto value set using default of 90 minutes.";end
	stackto_duration = 90
end
refreshto_duration = CharSettings["scrollbuff-refreshto"]
if debug == true;echo "Refresh duration: #{refreshto_duration}";end
if !(CharSettings["scrollbuff-refreshto"].to_i > 0)
	if debug == true; echo "Warning! No refreshto value set using default of 10 minutes.";end
	refreshto_duration = 10
end

##Check for script commands
SpellNums = script.vars[1..-1]
if SpellNums.nil? || SpellNums.count == 0 || SpellNums.first.start_with?("h")
    echofmt "Attempts to cast defensive or self-cast spells from your collection of scrolls, vellums, parchments, etc.",
			"Checks your reserve slots first -- reserved scrolls are invoked directly without needing",
			"to be held -- then will rummage in your scrollsack for matching spell numbers, upon finding",
			"a vibrant scroll it will place that scroll in your vibrantscrollsack unless usage of vibrant",
			"scrolls is toggled on.",
            "",
            "Before running, you must set your scrollsack and vibrantscrollsack with a command like:",
            "   ;vars set scrollsack=pouch",
            "   ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=black satchel",
            "",
			"You must have an empty right hand, or a non-scroll item in right hand and an empty left hand.",
            "",
			"The script will tell you which spells it cast and which it skipped.",
            "Casts stackable spells that are not running or have under",
            "#{stackto_duration} minutes left.  To change this setting enter:",
			"   ;#{script.name} stackto (minutes)",
            "",	
            "Casts refreshable spells that are not running or have under",
            "#{refreshto_duration} minutes left.  To change this setting enter:",
			"   ;#{script.name} refreshto (minutes)",
            "",				
			"Vibrant ink scrolls will be skipped by default and moved to your set vibrantscrollsack. If vibrant",	
			"toggle is on, will still prefer scrolls in scrollsack before checking vibrantscrollsack.",
			"To toggle use of vibrant ink scrolls enter: ",	
			"   ;#{script.name} vibrant",			
            "",
            "Usage: ;#{script.name} 101 107 509 ...",
            "List up to 30 spell numbers separated by a space.",
            "",
			"To list all relevant settings for this script:",
			"Current settings:"
			
			if (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True");usevibrant="True";else;usevibrant="No";end			
			echofmt "scrollsack: #{Vars["scrollsack"]}",
			"Vibrantscrollsack: #{Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]}",	
			"Use vibrant Scrolls: #{usevibrant}",	
			"Stack spells to: #{stackto_duration} minutes",
			"Refresh spells below: #{refreshto_duration} minutes"			


    exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("vibrant")
	if CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True"
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] = "False"
		echofmt "You are now set to NOT use vibrant ink scrolls.",
		"If a vibrant ink scroll is rummaged this script will put the scroll in your vibrantscrollsack and rummage again."
	else
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] = "True"
		echofmt "You are now set to use vibrant ink scrolls.",
		"If a vibrant ink scroll is rummaged this script will invoke it to absorb the spell's",
		"knowledge, then incant stackable spells until they hit their maximum duration",
		"(refreshable and one-shot spells are still just cast once)."
	end
	exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("stackto")
		if debug == true; echo "Second value: #{SpellNums[1]}";end
		if !(SpellNums[1].to_i > 0)
			echofmt "You need to specify a duration in minutes like:",
			"   ;#{script.name} stackto 30"	
			exit
		end
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-stackto"] = SpellNums[1]
		echofmt "You are now set invoke stackable spells until above #{SpellNums[1]} minutes." 
		exit
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("refreshto")
		if debug == true; echo "Second value: #{SpellNums[1]}";end
		if !(SpellNums[1].to_i > 0)
			echofmt "You need to specify a duration in minutes like:",
			"   ;#{script.name} refreshto 5"	
			exit
		end
		CharSettings["scrollbuff-refreshto"] = SpellNums[1]
		echofmt "You are now set invoke stackable spells until above #{SpellNums[1]} minutes." 
		exit		
elsif SpellNums.first.start_with?("settings")
	if (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True");usevibrant="True";else;usevibrant="No";end

	
	echofmt "scrollsack: #{Vars["scrollsack"]}",
			"Vibrantscrollsack: #{Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]}",	
			"Use vibrant Scrolls: #{usevibrant}",	
			"Stack spells to: #{stackto_duration} minutes",
			"Refresh spells below: #{refreshto_duration} minutes"			

	exit			
end

##Check for Vibrant Scroll Sack
vibrantscrollsackVar = Vars["vibrantscrollsack"]
unless (vibrantscrollsackVar || (CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True"))
    echofmt "You are not currently set to use vibrant ink scrolls.",
            "You need to set a place to store vibrant ink scrolls that are rummaged from your scrollsack.",
            "command like:",
            "    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=black backpack"
    
    exit
else
	vibrantscrollsack = GameObj[vibrantscrollsackVar]
	unless vibrantscrollsack
		echofmt "Couldn't find your vibrantscrollsack \"#{vibrantscrollsack}\"",
				"Fetch that and try again, would ya?"
		exit
	end
	if GameObj[vibrantscrollsackVar] == GameObj[scrollsackVar]
		echofmt "Your vibrantscrollsack must be a different container than your scrollsack",
				"Change one of the other to a different container and try again. Example:",
				"    ;vars set vibrantscrollsack=black backpack",
				"OR",
				"    ;vars set scrollsack=pouch"	
				exit
	end	
end


##Check list of spells for useability
## Use Spell.active (which relies on the self-healing active? check, same as ewaggle.lic)
## rather than the raw spell.active attribute, which can go stale.
active_spell_times = Hash[Spell.active.map { |s| [s.num.to_s, s.timeleft] }]

SpellNumsNeeded = SpellNums.find_all do |spell_num|
    spell = Spell[spell_num]
	if debug == true; echo "Availbility: #{spell.availability}";end
	next false unless spell && !(spell.type =~ /attack/)

	existing_duration = active_spell_times[spell.num.to_s] || 0
	if debug == true; echo "#{spell_num} existing duration: #{existing_duration}";end

	if spell.stackable?
		existing_duration <= stackto_duration.to_f
	elsif spell.refreshable?
		existing_duration <= refreshto_duration.to_f
	else
		existing_duration.zero?
	end
end

if SpellNumsNeeded.count.zero?
    echofmt "NO SPELLS NEEDED",
            "",
            "All spells are active with at least #{stackto_duration} minutes remaining."
    
    exit
end

## Make sure scroll sacks are open
fput "open ##{scrollsack.id}"
fput "open ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"

def findscroll(spell_num, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack)
	## Reserved scrolls can be invoked directly without ever being in hand.
	## Try those first before rummaging through the containers. Each reserve
	## item's spell is fixed for the life of the run, so once we've matched
	## one to a spell number, reuse that match instead of re-testing it
	## against every other spell number too.
	fput("reserve list") if GameObj.reserve.nil?
	if (known_id = $scrollbuff3_reserve_matches[spell_num.to_s])
		return ["reserve", known_id, nil]
	end
	already_matched = $scrollbuff3_reserve_matches.values
	GameObj.reserve.to_a.find_all { |o| o.noun =~ /scroll|paper|papyrus|parchment|vellum|palimpsest/i }.reject { |o| already_matched.include?(o.id) }.each do |candidate|
		result = dothis "invoke #{spell_num} from ##{candidate.id}", /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin.|and gesture to invoke the|That spell is not on the|Invoke from what/
		next if result =~ /That spell is not on the|Invoke from what/
		$scrollbuff3_reserve_matches[spell_num.to_s] = candidate.id
		return ["reserve", candidate.id, result]
	end

        result = dothis "rummage in ##{scrollsack.id} spell #{spell_num}", /You rummage through .+ (and remove .+ with .+ scrawled upon it|but can't seem to locate anything with that spell on it)/

        if result =~ /but can't seem to locate anything with that spell on it/
			if CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True"
				result = dothis "rummage in ##{vibrantscrollsack.id} spell #{spell_num}", /You rummage through .+ (and remove .+ with .+ scrawled upon it|but can't seem to locate anything with that spell on it)/
				if result =~ /but can't seem to locate anything with that spell on it/
					if debug == true; echo "Missing scroll for #{spell_num}";end
					return ["none", nil, nil]
				else
					scrollid = checkright ? GameObj.right_hand.id : GameObj.left_hand.id
					return ["vibrant", scrollid, nil]
				end
			end

			if debug == true; echo "Missing scroll for #{spell_num}";end
			return ["none", nil, nil]

		else
			## The first rummage already succeeded and put a scroll in hand.
			scrolltype = "normal"
			unless CharSettings["scrollbuff-usevibranttoggle"] == "True"
				scrolltype = ""
				until (scrolltype == "normal" || scrolltype == "none")
					if checkright =~ /scroll|paper|papyrus|parchment|vellum|palimpsest/			
						result = dothistimeout "read ##{GameObj.right_hand.id}", 0.5, /vibrant/
						if result =~ /vibrant/
							fput "put right in ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"
							scrolltype="vibrant"
						else
							scrolltype="normal"
						end
					elsif checkleft =~ /scroll|paper|papyrus|parchment|vellum|palimpsest/
						result = dothistimeout "read ##{GameObj.left_hand.id}", 0.5, /vibrant/
						if result =~ /vibrant/
							fput "put left in ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"
							scrolltype="vibrant"						
						else
							scrolltype="normal"
						end
					else
						if debug == true; echo "Error, no scroll found in hands when expected";end
						exit
					end
					if !(scrolltype == "normal")
						result = dothis "rummage in ##{scrollsack.id} spell #{spell_num}", /You rummage through .+ (and remove .+ with .+ scrawled upon it|but can't seem to locate anything with that spell on it)/
						if result =~ /but can't seem to locate anything with that spell on it/
							if debug == true; echo "missing scroll";end
							scrolltype = "none"
						end
					end
				end
			end
			scrollid = (scrolltype == "none") ? nil : (checkright ? GameObj.right_hand.id : GameObj.left_hand.id)
			return [scrolltype, scrollid, nil]
		end
end

def castscroll(spell_num, scrollid, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack, stackto_duration, refreshto_duration, scrolltype, prefetched_result = nil)

	if (Spell[spell_num].stackable?)
		if debug == true; echo "#{spell_num} is stackable";end
		## Vibrant scrolls grant temporary knowledge of the spell instead of consuming
		## a scroll per cast, so stack all the way to the spell's real max duration
		## rather than stopping at the (scroll-conserving) stackto_duration.
		target_duration = (scrolltype == "vibrant") ? Spell[spell_num].max_duration.to_f : stackto_duration.to_f
		if debug == true; echo (Spell[spell_num].timeleft >= target_duration);end
		if debug == true; echo scrolltype;end
	
		until ((Spell[spell_num].timeleft >= target_duration)||(scrolltype == "none"))
			if debug == true; echo "Current #{spell_num} duration: #{Spell[spell_num].timeleft}";end
			if Spell[spell_num].timeleft >= target_duration; echo "Spell already above target duration"; break; end
			waitcastrt?
			waitrt?							
			if prefetched_result
				result = prefetched_result
				prefetched_result = nil
			else
				result = dothis "invoke #{spell_num} from ##{scrollid}", /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin.|and gesture to invoke the|That spell is not on the|Invoke from what/
			end
			if result =~ /and gesture to invoke the/
				fput "cast"
			elsif result =~ /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin./
				## Guard against the spell's true server-enforced cap being lower than
				## target_duration (e.g. missing/incorrect max data): if a cast doesn't
				## actually add duration, we've hit the real cap, so stop instead of
				## incanting forever.
				until (Spell[spell_num].timeleft >= target_duration)
					previous_duration = Spell[spell_num].timeleft
					if !(Spell[spell_num].affordable?); echo "waiting for mana...";end
					wait_until { Spell[spell_num].affordable? }				
					waitcastrt?
					waitrt?					
					fput "incant #{spell_num}" if Spell[spell_num].affordable?
					waitcastrt?
					waitrt?									
					## The duration feed can lag a beat behind the cast confirmation, so
					## give it a few seconds to catch up before concluding the spell is
					## capped and it's time to stop incanting.
					made_progress = false
					6.times do
						break if (made_progress = Spell[spell_num].timeleft > previous_duration + 0.5)
						sleep 0.5
					end
					unless made_progress
						if debug == true; echo "#{spell_num} duration did not increase (#{Spell[spell_num].timeleft} min), stopping at the real cap";end
						break
					end
				end
			elsif result =~ /That spell is not on the|Invoke from what/
				if scrolltype == "reserve"
					## Never picked up -- nothing to put away.
				elsif scrolltype == "vibrant"
					if GameObj.right_hand.id == scrollid
						fput "put right in ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"
					elsif GameObj.left_hand.id == scrollid
						fput "put left in ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"
					end
				else
					if GameObj.right_hand.id == scrollid
						fput "put right in ##{scrollsack.id}"
					elsif GameObj.left_hand.id == scrollid
						fput "put left in ##{scrollsack.id}"
					end
				end
				scrolltype, scrollid, prefetched_result = findscroll(spell_num, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack)
				target_duration = (scrolltype == "vibrant") ? Spell[spell_num].max_duration.to_f : stackto_duration.to_f
			end
			waitcastrt?
			waitrt?					
		end

		
	elsif (Spell[spell_num].refreshable?)
		if debug == true; echo "#{spell_num} is refreshable";end
		if debug == true; echo "Current #{spell_num} duration: #{Spell[spell_num].timeleft}";end
			if Spell[spell_num].timeleft < refreshto_duration.to_f
				waitcastrt?
				waitrt?							
				result = prefetched_result || dothis("invoke #{spell_num} from ##{scrollid}", /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin.|and gesture to invoke the|That spell is not on the|Invoke from what/)
				if result =~ /and gesture to invoke the/
					fput "cast"
				elsif result =~ /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin./
					if !(Spell[spell_num].affordable?); echo "waiting for mana...";end
					wait_until { Spell[spell_num].affordable? }
					waitcastrt?
					waitrt?					
					fput "incant #{spell_num}" if Spell[spell_num].affordable?
					waitcastrt?
					waitrt?											
				end
				waitcastrt?
				waitrt?			else
				if debug == true; echo "Spell already above refresh to duration";end
			end
		
	else
		if debug == true;echo "Scroll is not stackable or refreshable, casting once";end
				waitcastrt?
				waitrt?							
				result = prefetched_result || dothis("invoke #{spell_num} from ##{scrollid}", /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin.|and gesture to invoke the|That spell is not on the|Invoke from what/)
				if result =~ /and gesture to invoke the/
					fput "cast"
				elsif result =~ /As you begin your invocation the ink leaps from the page and seeps into your skin./
					if !(Spell[spell_num].affordable?); echo "waiting for mana...";end
					wait_until { Spell[spell_num].affordable? }
					waitcastrt?
					waitrt?					
					fput "incant #{spell_num}" if Spell[spell_num].affordable?
					waitcastrt?
					waitrt?											
				end
				waitcastrt?
				waitrt?
	end
     
	## The scroll may have already been put away (e.g. by the "That spell is
	## not on the ..." retry above), or may have come from reserve and never
	## been picked up at all -- only put it away here if it's still in a hand.
	if [GameObj.right_hand.id, GameObj.left_hand.id].include?(scrollid)
		if scrolltype == "vibrant"
			fput "put ##{scrollid} in ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"
		else
			fput "put ##{scrollid} in ##{scrollsack.id}"
		end
	end
end

spells_cast = []
spells_not_found = []

SpellNumsNeeded.each do |spell_num|

    spell = Spell[spell_num]

    if spell && !(spell.type =~ /attack/)

		scrolltype, scrollid, prefetched_result = findscroll(spell_num, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack)

		if scrolltype == "none" || scrollid.nil?
			echo "No scroll found for #{spell_num} #{spell.name}, skipping."
			spells_not_found << spell_num
		else
			castscroll(spell_num, scrollid, scrollsack, vibrantscrollsack, stackto_duration, refreshto_duration, scrolltype, prefetched_result)
			spells_cast << spell_num
		end

    else
		echo "Not a viable spell type"
	end

end

##fput "close ##{scrollsack.id}"
##fput "close ##{vibrantscrollsack.id}"

echofmt "SCROLL BUFFS COMPLETE",
        "",
        "Spells cast: #{spells_cast.join(" ")}",
        "Spells not found: #{spells_not_found.join(" ")}",
        "Spells not needed: #{(SpellNums - SpellNumsNeeded).join(" ")}"
